        "original_id": "793cd180-9027-5e1a-b0e7-4663c1b51385",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sophie Ellis-Bextor, Jo Kwon, Ga-in\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, model, MC, actor, entertainer, boy band leader\n- Organizations: 2AM, Mnet Asian Music Awards\n- Awards: Mnet Asian Music Award for Best Collaboration\n- Songs: Get Over You, Move This Mountain, We Fell in Love\n- Topics: British pop music, South Korean music collaboration\n\nFacts:\n- Sophie Michelle Ellis-Bextor was born on 10 April 1979 and is an English singer, songwriter, and model.\n- Jo Kwon was born on August 28, 1989 and is a South Korean singer, MC, actor, entertainer, and the leader of the South Korean boy band 2AM.\n- The Mnet Asian Music Award for Best Collaboration was first awarded at the 12th Mnet Asian Music Awards ceremony in 2010.\n- Ga-in and Jo Kwon won the 2010 Mnet Asian Music Award for Best Collaboration for the song \"We Fell in Love.\"\n- The Mnet Asian Music Award for Best Collaboration honors artists with the most artistic achievement in collaboration performances in the music industry.\n- \"Get Over You\" and \"Move This Mountain\" are songs recorded by British pop singer Sophie Ellis-Bextor.",
